+## OpenCode Go: one subscription, three protocols
+
+[`opencode-go`](./opencode-go.md), `opencode-go-responses` and `opencode-go-messages` are one
+product: OpenCode's flat-rate subscription, billed by an API key, whose catalog is served across
+the three protocols meka speaks. Which backend a model needs is OpenCode's routing, not meka's;
+pick the backend whose protocol the model is served on. Every request these backends send carries
+the conversation's id in `x-opencode-session`, which the gateway requires.
+
 ## Streaming vs non-streaming

 By default, meka uses streaming mode: tokens appear in the terminal as they are generated. Use `--no-stream` to wait for the complete response before displaying it.
